    "description": "Infirmary, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). Over budget: 463 blocks vs 285 (first build 389 vs 235). White plaster ward in a dark oak frame under a spruce gable roof, a red wool cross on white in the front gable: six beds (three on each side, heads to the wall, a window over each), bedside tables, a hearth, herb barrels and shelves, a lean-to herb store; L2 adds the brewing stand and cauldron, candles, lanterns, flower boxes, a door canopy and the banner; L3 a herb garden, herb pots, more banners, a bench and a lantern post.",
    "changes": "The red cross now reads as one: red wool on a white wool field in the front gable overhang (QC: the brick cross looked like chimney masonry); L1 gets a bench and a planter by the front, L2 sills under the side and back windows, L3 lanterns on the herb-bed end posts.",
